people are going to complain to their friends and family. And then those friends and family will complain about it to somebody else. And so what starts as one person can become a much bigger group. So I think they probably are more concerned than it appears that they are. I think a lot of us have the impression that people are more likely to post something negative. They complain when they're unhappy rather than posting something on social media where they feel good about things. And is that just an impression or is it really true that we're much more motivated to get out there and say something bad than we are to get out there and say something good? I think it depends on the person. I'm not somebody who posts a lot anyway.

