31
00:18:56.000 --> 00:19:26.000
doing. And then those are the kinds of things that people will oftentimes post on social media. Again, I think it's usually to just get some validation of, oh, yeah, me too, or this is how I resolve that or whatever it is. So I think that's part of what motivates the negative complaining. What about advice for someone who feels like they complain too much and they want to dial it back? I mean, what are the things that people can do besides that risk ban that you mention, other other things? So, but it relates to the wristband. So it's truly being mindful. The other thing I would do is I think journaling is really important.

32
00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:56.000
You know, and I know I mentioned this earlier, but, you know, when we have things in our head, It's like that mountain out of a molehill thing. Things in our head seem just so big and, oh, just I, you know, it's like if you have a list of things to do, it's just like, I have such a huge list until you write it down, and then it doesn't seem quite as overwhelming. Well, it's the same way with our sources of dissatisfaction. And oftentimes, particularly if you're a chronic complainer, I think journaling can be very important, you know, because we can take all the dissatisfaction that's in our head and

33
00:19:56.000 --> 00:20:31.000
we can get it down on the computer or on a piece of paper. And I do, I still think there's value in writing. writing things out by hand. But whatever, wherever you put it, wherever you write it, at least it gets that jamble out of our head where we're mulling it over and making it bigger than it should be. And, you know, when we articulate it in writing, it loses some of its potency. And I think that it's a very effective technique for dealing with complaining for anybody, but especially for chronic complainers who detect that they are wearing out their audience.

34
00:20:31.000 --> 00:20:56.000
You know, they know they're not complaining effectively. They're starting to wear on people. And I think it increases their mindfulness because if they're journaling about their complaining, then they realize how much they're complaining. So I think it's a highly effective technique. And do you try to counterbalance that with some positive things while you're journaling? Oh, absolutely. And honestly, the journaling ultimately leads to more, you know,

